Dang.

Wouldn't you know it?  In my rush to get the NetHack-- 3.1.3 patch out
to all of the people waiting with baited breath, I did something really
stupid.  Ah well.

The NetHack-- 3.1.3 patch posted to rec.games.hack and alt.sources a few
days ago has a problem...  It's got DOS end-of-lines.  Silly me.

This means the patch will fail on all unix systems, and probably most
other systems that don't waste extra characters for end-of-line.

How can you fix this problem?

a) use Rahul Desi's "flip" program:
	flip -u NH31C--.Patch
   will fix your problems.  Apply the patch and go nuts.

b) Load NH31C--.Patch (or NH31C--.PAT or whatever) into a decent text
   editor, like emacs.  Replace <NL><NL> with <NL>.

c) Wait for me to post the patch as a three-part shar file.

Sorry about the wasted bandwidth.  The shar files take up less space
than the uuencoded tar file (well, when it's going between systems
anyway), but it's still a pain.  I hope that not too many people have
wasted some time on this.

